Article 26

1. Implementation of Protection for women victims of violence in order to provide legal protection and/or health recovery (2) Protection for women victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. legal aid;
b. assistance after the occurrence of acts of violence; c. rehabilitation and social reintegration; and d. health services.

Article 16

Implementation of protection of women is provided to: a. female workers / laborers;
b. elderly women;
c. women with disabilities;
d. homeless women;
e. domestic workers;
f. women as family economic supporters;
g. women former inmates of correctional institutions; h. women victims of disasters;
i. female commercial sex workers; andj. women victims of violence.

REGENT OF SOUTH BANGKA,

Considering:
a. that women and men have equal rights to participate in various fields of life;
b. that women are a national asset who play a very important role in the process of continuation and creation of quality generations, therefore they need to receive protection guarantees from acts of violence and discrimination and need to be empowered so that they can actualize their potential optimally;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Empowerment and Protection of Women;

In View of:
1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 1 of 1974 concerning Marriage (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1974 Number 1, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3019);
3. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on The Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);

