Article 4

Women's Empowerment and Protection aims to: a. increase women's participation in the development process;
b. improve the quality of life of women;
c. provide guarantees to women in the fulfillment of their rights as human beings;andd. provide a sense of security by increasing protection for women from various acts of violence.

Article 20

1. Implementation of protection for homeless women in order to provide protection and prevention against forms of violence caused by the absence of shelter or permanent residence.
2. Homeless women as referred to in paragraph (1) receive the right to protection over:a. decent housing;
b. health and social security;
c. population administration registration;
d. opportunities to obtain skills to improve economic status; ande. access to information and legal consultation services.

CHAPTER XII

GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION

Article 32

1. The Regent or OPD responsible for women's empowerment shall conduct guidance and supervision over the empowerment and protection of women;
2. The forms of guidance as referred to in paragraph (1) are as follows:a. provide socialization to the community and business sector regarding policies on women's empowerment and protection;
b. provide books, leaflets, brochures regarding women's empowerment and protection, and other related issues and disseminate them to the community;

c facilitate capacity building of institutions implementing women's empowerment and protection;
d. facilitate forums for women's participation and women's organizations;
e. facilitate rehabilitation and reintegration services for women victims of disasters and victims of violence;
f. coordinate the participation of the business sector and other institutions, including international assistance for women's empowerment and protection;andg. provide awards to the community and business sector both individually and institutionally who have made efforts in women's empowerment and protection.
3. The form of supervision as referred to in paragraph (1) may be in the form of monitoring and evaluation activities on women's empowerment and protection.

Article 19

1. Implementation of Protection for women with disabilities in order to provide protection and prevention against forms of discrimination including freedom from cruel, inhumane treatment, degrading human dignity and freedom from exploitation;
2. Women with disabilities as referred to in paragraph (1) receive the right to protection over: a. guarantee of continuity and personal self-development;

www.jdih.bangkaselatankab.go.id
b. participation in the fields of education, health, employment, politics, sports, arts and culture as well as utilization of information and communication technology;
c. accessibility to information, legal aid, mobility, social services; andd. early intervention efforts including treatment and rehabilitation to improve their function and capacity.

CHAPTER IV

WOMEN'S RIGHTS

Article 5

1. Every woman has the right to:a. live and maintain life and improve her standard of living;
b. fulfill her basic needs to grow and develop properly, have a family and continue offspring;
c. develop her personality, to obtain education, and improve her quality of life to become a human being who is faithful, pious, responsible, noble, happy, and prosperous in accordance with human rights;
d. obtain justice, security, and freedom to express opinions without discrimination;
e. be involved in every stage of the development process; f. be free from slavery or servitude and threats; g. obtain protection of her person, family, honor, dignity and property rights;

www.jdih.bangkaselatankab.go.id
h. obtain welfare and a decent life; i. participate in politics;
j. perform legal acts; andk. freely choose a partner in her marriage. (2) Every wife during the marriage bond has the same rights and responsibilities as her husband over all matters relating to their married life, relations with their children, and ownership and management of joint property in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.
3. After the dissolution of marriage, a woman has rights and responsibilities with her former husband over all matters relating to children with due regard to the best interests of the child.

CHAPTER II

SCOPE

Article 2

The scope of this Regional Regulation includes:
a. Principles and objectives;
b. Women's rights;
c. Obligations and Responsibilities of the Regional Government; d. Women's Empowerment;
e. Women's Protection;
f. Strategy for Women's Empowerment and Protection; g. Mechanism for Implementation of Women's Empowerment and Protection;
h. Community Participation;
i. Funding; andj. Guidance and Supervision.

