CHAPTER IV

WOMEN'S RIGHTS

Article 5

1. Every woman has the right to:a. live and maintain life and improve her standard of living;
b. fulfill her basic needs to grow and develop properly, have a family and continue offspring;
c. develop her personality, to obtain education, and improve her quality of life to become a human being who is faithful, pious, responsible, noble, happy, and prosperous in accordance with human rights;
d. obtain justice, security, and freedom to express opinions without discrimination;
e. be involved in every stage of the development process; f. be free from slavery or servitude and threats; g. obtain protection of her person, family, honor, dignity and property rights;

www.jdih.bangkaselatankab.go.id
h. obtain welfare and a decent life; i. participate in politics;
j. perform legal acts; andk. freely choose a partner in her marriage. (2) Every wife during the marriage bond has the same rights and responsibilities as her husband over all matters relating to their married life, relations with their children, and ownership and management of joint property in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.
3. After the dissolution of marriage, a woman has rights and responsibilities with her former husband over all matters relating to children with due regard to the best interests of the child.

